%I A398825 #7 Aug 12 2026 01:36:35
%S A398825 1,2,5,6,10,13,14,15,16,21,22,29,30,33,34,37,38,41,42,46,47,57,58,61,
%T A398825 65,66,69,70,73,77,78,79,80,81,82,85,86,93,94,101,102,105,106,109,110,
%U A398825 111,112,113,114,118,122,127,128,129,130,133,137,138,141,142,145
%N A398825 Numbers k such that the canonical prime factorizations of both k and k+1 contain only exponents that are congruent to 1 modulo 3.
%C A398825 Numbers k such that k and k+1 are both terms in A366762.
%C A398825 Differs from A398166 by having the terms 127, 128, 383, 384, 640, 895, 896, ..., and not having the terms 511, 1535, 1536, 2559, 2560, ... .
%C A398825 The asymptotic density of this sequence is d = zeta(3) * Product_{p prime} (1 - 2/p^2 - 1/p^3 + 2/p^4) = 0.3782601715591552459004... . The number of terms not exceeding x is d * x + O(x^(2/3+eps)), where eps > 0 (Srichan et al., 2026, a consequence of Theorem 1.1).
%H A398825 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A398825/b398825.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A398825 Teerapat Srichan, Nithi Rungtanapirom, and Saeree Wananiyakul, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1051/ita/2026022">On the distribution of consecutive M-free integers</a>, RAIRO - Theoretical Informatics and Applications, Vol. 60 (2026), Article 22.
%e A398825 15 = 3^1 * 5^1 is a term since its prime factorization exponents are two 1's, and 1 == 1 (mod 3), and the prime factorization exponent of 15 + 1 = 16 = 2^4 is 4, and 4 == 1 (mod 3).
%t A398825 a366762Q[k_] := a366762Q[k] = AllTrue[FactorInteger[k][[;; , 2]], Mod[#, 3] == 1 &]; Select[Range[150], a366762Q[#] && a366762Q[#+1] &]
%o A398825 (PARI) isA366762(k) = {my(f = factor(k)); for(i = 1, #f~, if(f[i, 2]%3 != 1, return(0))); 1;}
%o A398825 isok(k) = isA366762(k) && isA366762(k+1);
%Y A398825 Subsequence of A366762.
%Y A398825 A007674 is a subsequence.
%Y A398825 Cf. A002117, A016777.
%Y A398825 Similar sequences: A007674, A340152, A367695, A372690, A391396, A398161, A398162, A398163, A398164, A398165, A398166, A398167, A398168, A398169, A398170.
%K A398825 nonn,easy
%O A398825 1,2
